title The meter that could not see a type, and the queue it had been ordering on half a cost
prompt Autonomous loop -- Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Caravan fold arc
think Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first, then REMEMBER, the three itineraries, and the top rows of the log index. The running thread named judge_outcome at 468 as the next fold head.
think Standfast pass over crux/REDS.md -- rows %137, %138, %139 all booked AND closed. Line clear for constructive work.
think Council rota lap index: git log holds 3277 commits, 3277 mod 5 = 2, so row 2 -- Fire/Mars, cut and stop: standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal.
think Measured judge_outcome before lifting it. The scan reported widens=37, every one a free import binding of carry, which caravan/ladder_checks.rye already imports at line 54 -- so the row read free.
think Then read the body by hand. Its parameter type is `Finished`, and `Finished` stands `const` rather than `pub const` in all thirty-seven rungs. A meter that had just read that body reported nothing to widen.
think Built a two-rung control in /tmp sharing one body over a private `Ledger`. The scan answered reached=0 widens=0 -- not a zero cost, a blindness. REDS %140 booked.
think Root: both halves of the join used the character class [a-z_]. The body's identifier grep read [a-z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]* and the declaration reader matched /^(pub )?(fn|const) [a-z_]/. Zig type names are capitalized without exception on this ladder, so no type was ever seen from either side.
think Repair on metal: both classes widened to [A-Za-z_], and a fourth generated control joined the scan's own prove-red roster asserting widens=2 widens_const=2 on the exact reading the blind meter got wrong.
think Re-priced the whole queue under the corrected meter. Only two rows moved -- judge_outcome 37 to 74, may_pass 96 to 101 -- which is the evidence the correction found real cost rather than manufacturing it.
think The queue reordered, and that reordering chose the lap. case_path returns 462 for zero widenings of every kind; judge_outcome returns six more lines bought with thirty-seven struct openings. Took the free row.
obs A compiler is a real backstop -- a lift reaching a private type simply refuses to build -- yet it fires AFTER the queue has been ordered, and the ordering is the decision the meter exists to inform. A blindness that costs nothing on the lap it fires still costs the choice it silently made.
obs case_path is twenty-five lines over a one-line signature, the longest single body this arc has lifted and, by the corrected meter, the cheapest. Length and cost stay separate facts, exactly as the split widening column keeps saying.
obs All twenty-two declarers folded and none stayed home -- the first family since load_one where no rung had a structural reason to keep its body.
obs Two witnesses carried the blind number in their own asserts and both went RED on the corrected scan, which is the guard apparatus working: the meter changed and the pins refused to agree until they were read again.
